From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:52:43 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] WebGL on Windows 10 Mobile at feature level 9_3, behind a
 pref

ANGLE's D3D11 renderer asked for feature level 10_0 and up only, so at 9_3
(Lumia 550, 650, 950) WebGL fell to WARP, a CPU rasteriser on four Cortex-A7
cores. ANGLE now also accepts 9_3 (last in the list, so higher levels are
unchanged), and its clear shaders get level_9_3 forms again
(Clear11_FL9.hlsl, compiled with fxc vs/ps_4_0_level_9_3): upstream had
dropped them, and every masked or scissored clear failed. WebGL 2 is never
offered at 9_3. webgl.gecko-w10m.feature-level-9, off by default until the
cost of pages probing WebGL is measured on a Lumia, decides whether WebGL 1
runs there; off, getContext fails at once and nothing is loaded. WARP is no
longer taken silently (webgl.forbid-software), and failIfMajorPerformanceCaveat
is honoured. Accelerated canvas 2D is turned off at 9_3: it draws through
WebGL 2. gfxPlatform also says whether the shader cache is on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
